# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Cloned corpus repos. Reproducible from the slugs in the manifests, and far too
# large to version (543MB for five repos).
.cache/

# Mined label sets from v2 onward. These are *derived* data: the deterministic
# output of (repo shas, commit window, MineConfig, code version), and one day of
# iteration produced seven of them totalling 16MB. What gets versioned instead is
# the provenance -- `data/*.manifest.json` records every input plus a sha256 of
# the output, and its `replay` field regenerates the file byte-identically. That
# was verified, not assumed, before this rule was added.
#
# `data/labels.jsonl` (v1) is deliberately NOT ignored. It predates manifests, so
# it is the one label set that cannot be regenerated, and the hand-labelled
# verdicts in review/ join to it by `example_id`. Losing it would make the
# ground-truth sheets unattributable.
data/labels-v*.jsonl

# Never ignored, and worth saying why:
#   review/*.md              -- the hand labels. Irreplaceable; every number
#                               downstream is measured against them.
#   data/scores/*.json       -- the measurement history. A result is data, not
#                               console output.
#   data/*.manifest.json     -- what makes the ignored files above regenerable.
